                                        "entry_id": "08102bf3-433e-33b9-8819-6d936484c19b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "In screw theory, a screw assembled from force and torque vectors arising from application of Newton's laws to a rigid body."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1c7c0762-0241-313d-b8f7-792b72564764",
                                        "entry_id": "08102bf3-433e-33b9-8819-6d936484c19b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "means; contrivance"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "44c4313c-86f7-4998-9163-161894732edc",
                                                "sense_id": "1c7c0762-0241-313d-b8f7-792b72564764",
                                                "text": "But weighing one thing with another he gave Britain for lost; but resolved to make his profit of this business of Britain, as a quarrel for war; and that of Naples, as a wrench and mean for peace"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8c957cbc-c6c3-3f9e-af98-d97ab6494106",
                                        "entry_id": "08102bf3-433e-33b9-8819-6d936484c19b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "In coursing, the act of bringing the hare round at less than a right angle, worth half a point in the recognised code of points for judging."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "wrench",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5e44a04c-564e-376f-8729-dc6b8157b37c",
                                        "entry_id": "89996156-f852-3da7-aaf8-09e2301a2534",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To pull or twist violently."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "756ef46e-4a75-4d16-8689-4acaab7e6c7f",
                                                "sense_id": "5e44a04c-564e-376f-8729-dc6b8157b37c",
                                                "text": "With a surge of adrenaline, she wrenched the car door off and pulled out the injured man."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "41ce3972-bf51-398f-9b3c-77a815c0e27e",
                                        "entry_id": "89996156-f852-3da7-aaf8-09e2301a2534",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To injure (a joint) by pulling or twisting."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8b02fefd-46d7-44b8-bf16-2ef423148fce",
                                                "sense_id": "41ce3972-bf51-398f-9b3c-77a815c0e27e",
                                                "text": "Be careful not to wrench your ankle walking along those loose stones!"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1c187a06-be4d-3a82-bb01-80639d2ffb39",
                                        "entry_id": "89996156-f852-3da7-aaf8-09e2301a2534",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To distort the original meaning of; to misrepresent."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "680e3168-ca0a-3b79-a5ee-6123022e75e0",
                                        "entry_id": "89996156-f852-3da7-aaf8-09e2301a2534",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To rack with pain; to make hurt or distressed."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a295ba7f-3773-4103-9b92-1201ab082274",
                                                "sense_id": "680e3168-ca0a-3b79-a5ee-6123022e75e0",
                                                "text": "And what actinic, mind-wrenching form could the countermeme take? How could human hands assemble something so devastatingly powerful and hold it steady; what human mind could wield it without exploding from the inside out?"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9125a20e-fb4c-3fc6-842c-9eebea4a2804",
                                        "entry_id": "89996156-f852-3da7-aaf8-09e2301a2534",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To deprive by means of a violent pull or twist."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "53c8ce73-f399-3726-94c6-998e3f292b3a",
                                        "entry_id": "89996156-f852-3da7-aaf8-09e2301a2534",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To use a wrench; to twist with a wrench."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e23ec31f-00d2-45e1-abc8-7a3289fba7fb",
                                                "sense_id": "53c8ce73-f399-3726-94c6-998e3f292b3a",
                                                "text": "The plumber wrenched the pipes until they came loose."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b563c26d-45a0-3949-8f4e-e7f8c151e8c1",
                                        "entry_id": "89996156-f852-3da7-aaf8-09e2301a2534",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To violently move in a turn or writhe."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive",
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "72a7f6e8-24be-33ba-a61d-2644c59d656f",
                                        "entry_id": "89996156-f852-3da7-aaf8-09e2301a2534",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To tighten with or as if with a winch."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "obsolete",
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c695f016-ea2e-434a-b073-7a2b477552e5",
                                                "sense_id": "72a7f6e8-24be-33ba-a61d-2644c59d656f",
                                                "text": "[S]end me that hag hither; she shall avouch what it was that she hath given to the wretch Dryfesdale, or the pilniewinks and thumbikins shall wrench it out of her finger-joints."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7f3524d7-7956-3569-b8c0-71882b8faeb2",
                                        "entry_id": "89996156-f852-3da7-aaf8-09e2301a2534",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To thrust (a weapon) in a twisting motion."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "obsolete",
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "77308fb4-10b3-36df-a5cf-c953e94033a9",
                                        "entry_id": "89996156-f852-3da7-aaf8-09e2301a2534",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To disarm an opponent by whirling their blade away."
                                        ],
